schema: spec-driven

context: |
  Home Assistant App for the UniFi Poller application. This app collects data
  from a UniFi Network Controller and exports it to InfluxDB or Prometheus,
  where it can be visualised using Grafana.

  The external databases (InfluxDB or Prometheus) can be hosted either
  externally or via other Home Assistant Apps, depending on the deployment
  model.

  Home Assistant Apps (formerly known as add-ons) extend the functionality of
  Home Assistant by allowing additional services and applications to run
  alongside the core system. Apps are configured via the Supervisor panel.

  Configuration Approach:
    Configuration is designed to be flexible while remaining easy to use.
    The add-on leverages the standard Home Assistant add-on configuration
    file structure, allowing users to define options in a consistent and
    predictable way. Sensible defaults should be provided where possible,
    with the ability to override settings as needed for more advanced use
    cases.

  Under the hood, apps are distributed as container images published to
  registries such as GitHub Container Registry or Docker Hub. Developers can
  group multiple apps within a single repository for easier distribution and
  community sharing.

  Development Approach:
  https://developers.home-assistant.io/docs/apps/

  Tech Stack:
    - Bash
    - jq
    - yq
    - Docker
    - GitHub
    - GitHub Actions

  Docker:
    Base image: ghcr.io/home-assistant/base:latest
    Architecture: amd64

  CI/CD:
    GitHub Actions is used to build, validate, and package the app.
    JSON and YAML files are validated using jq and yq.

  Packaging:
    The Unpoller binary is written in Go and sourced from the official
    Unpoller GitHub repository. Built images are published to GitHub
    Container Registry.

  Versioning:
    Uses the upstream UniFi Poller version with an additional suffix
    for the add-on version.
    Example:
      Upstream version: v2.9.0
      Add-on version:  v2.9.0-1

  Documentation:
    Maintained as Markdown files in the root of the repository.

  Additional References:
    - Home Assistant Apps Tutorial:
      https://developers.home-assistant.io/docs/apps/tutorial
    - Unpoller Documentation and Releases:
      https://github.com/unpoller/unpoller
